#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "76450310-bc86-5f3b-9bb8-82206d89c627" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Left and Right Limits at an Interior Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b86b072-1562-55da-91a4-27882263519e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b86b072-1562-55da-91a4-27882263519e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245028} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a733054-678a-54d1-a44b-0ee24aae3ca2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "962fb48d-941a-571a-a27e-ca575aad3db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "962fb48d-941a-571a-a27e-ca575aad3db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245030} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97e9eb0-eaf6-5792-a7aa-af1d24e19f02" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa954449-631f-56d8-a490-f4aa6d55e8fe" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-131476" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932295/assets/e489437aa3b22a90d71dea3d30ff7a53bb800580775666f97dd4a6cf2db76e6d.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x).$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $-1$ from the left, the function $g(x)$ approaches $2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=2.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the right, the function $g(x)$ approaches $0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=2,\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2b72a2-c486-5a7a-a65e-57e83b78f6cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Limit at an Interior Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfcad43a-a4c5-5463-859a-50cc2fc044f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfcad43a-a4c5-5463-859a-50cc2fc044f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245033} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b75861-0df0-5d7a-aa65-6fb2c2acfcb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245032}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cf8aff3-674e-56cc-82b0-81f8c6a8e7a8" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-131477" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932295/assets/e489437aa3b22a90d71dea3d30ff7a53bb800580775666f97dd4a6cf2db76e6d.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x).$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we showed that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=2,\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x),$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2b72a2-c486-5a7a-a65e-57e83b78f6cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Limit at an Interior Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "402e2cb6-b1d8-5c91-a80b-c2eaa38d9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "402e2cb6-b1d8-5c91-a80b-c2eaa38d9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245036} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a0b342d-3844-53d5-9b72-f8d46b6aa8e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58ea61fc-07a6-5a58-b055-52c72f136884" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-131478" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932295/assets/e489437aa3b22a90d71dea3d30ff7a53bb800580775666f97dd4a6cf2db76e6d.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x).$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        DNE\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we see that as we approach $x=2$ from the left, the $y$-value approaches $-1.$ So the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}g(x)=-1.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, when we approach $x=2$ from the right, the $y$-value again approaches $-1.$ So the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}g(x)=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince both the left and right-hand limits exist and are equal to $-1,$ we conclude that\n\n \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea4038bf-34f0-58cc-a7b6-6a4c1890570f" :knowledge-point/title "The Limit at Infinity for an Unbounded Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d4d2b58-f3c9-5583-8ac5-76858282b532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d4d2b58-f3c9-5583-8ac5-76858282b532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245039} :answer-field/id #uuid "0928ec8c-abcd-539c-87f4-0a6ef78d2ff5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a0c0622-ed72-5243-920c-456f0841bfa9" :answer/ty